    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today with a aggressive stance on speed, headlined by **Corbin Carroll** (79.46) and **Jose Caballero** (75.83), our premier threats against left-handed pitching. **Corbin Carroll** is our highest-scored asset despite the L/L matchup against Abbott, as his dynamic speed and #2 spot in the order remain elite generators for our R and SB requirements. Meanwhile, **Jose Caballero** benefits from a massive 13% platoon adjustment against Corbin, making him a cornerstone play. **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91) also lands in the \"Strong\" category; while he faces the crafty Sugano, the combination of a favorable R/R platoon edge and the #3 lineup spot makes him a high-floor producer for our RBI total today.\n\nWe are forced to navigate thin margins with the remainder of our MI and C2 slots, specifically regarding **Max Muncy** (57.67) and **Kyle Karros** (54.63). **Max Muncy** narrowly missed the 60+ threshold as he operates against the steady arm of Sugano, but he remains in the lineup due to his power potential relative to our other available reserves. The most contentious bench decision was choosing **Kyle Karros** over our other depth options; while **Kyle Karros** is a marginal start, his +7% platoon boost against Springs was the tie-breaker over guys like **Zach McKinstry** or **Trevor Story**, who lack similar daily efficiency scores today. We continue to monitor the status of **Seiya Suzuki**, who remains benched, while our long-term IL stash trio of **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** continue their recovery. \n\nWe must remain cautious with **Dalton Rushing** (44.94) and **Austin Riley** (53.34), both of whom are fighting against stiff opposition. **Dalton Rushing** is saddled with an L/L disadvantage against Hudson, lowering his value, while **Austin Riley** is struggling against the elite arm of Peralta, whose 3.90 xERA is the toughest test for our offense today. Owners should keep an eye on **James Wood** (65.20); despite facing a pitcher with a 44% SB-prevention rate, his elite 0.403 xwOBA and lead-off positioning make him a locked-in starter. With **Brice Turang**, **Henry Bolte**, **Carson Williams**, and **Travis Bazzana** currently on the periphery of our active plans, we are confident this lineup maximizes our reach for the scarce SB category while maintaining viable scoring potential.",
